      # Reconstruction brief — proj
      
      This document was generated from ddflow's event log by `ddflow replay`. It is
      the complete decision history of the project: every operator instruction, every
      research verdict, every lesson, and the shape of the work queue.
      
      **How to use it.** Hand it to a coding agent with an empty repository and ask it
      to work through the instructions in order. It will not reproduce the original
      source byte-for-byte — model outputs are not deterministic — but it has every
      input that produced the original, which no other artefact does.
      
      - Phases: 1
      - Tasks: 3
      - Lessons carried forward: 1
      - Architectural decisions in force: 1
      - Research notes: 1 (1 confirmed, 0 refuted)
      
      ## Architectural decisions in force
      
      These bind the rebuild. They are the part no other artefact records: source
      code shows what was built and never why, nor what was rejected on the way.
      
      - **Hand-written parser** — Recursive descent, no generator
        - governs: src/**
      
      ## Standing knowledge — read before starting
      
      These were learned the hard way during the original build. They are inputs,
      not history: applying them is how the rebuild avoids repeating the mistakes.
      
      - **Pin the grammar before refactoring it** — Snapshot parser output first
      
      ## The instruction history
      
      ### 1. [PHASE] 2026-01-01T00:01:00Z — `P1`
      
      P1: Ship the parser
      
